.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH bap-run 1  "bap-run " 
.SH NAME
bap\-run \- Run a JavaScript or TypeScript file (bare `bap run` picks one)
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBbap\-run\fR [\fB\-\-no\-proofs\fR] [\fB\-\-require\-proofs\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fIFILE\fR] [\fISCRIPT_ARGS\fR] 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Run a JavaScript or TypeScript file (bare `bap run` picks one)
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-proofs\fR
Never consult the TypeScript proof backend
.TP
\fB\-\-require\-proofs\fR
Fail when a recognized proof candidate does not prove
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
[\fIFILE\fR]
Path to a JavaScript or TypeScript file
.TP
[\fISCRIPT_ARGS\fR]
arguments passed to the script (use `\-\-` before dash\-args)
.SH EXTRA
Examples:
  bap run server.js \-\- port 8080
  bap run            # runs the only script in this directory
  bap run \-\-require\-proofs route.ts
